# Project Purpose

- Speed up prototype design and authoring of UI definitions.
- Treat abstracted **IR (Intermediate Representation)** kinds as the domain core and **SSOT (Single Source Of Truth)**.
- Use those IR models to convert to/from UI-framework (and other vendor) definition files.
- Maximize portability; minimize dependence on specific tech stacks or platform vendors.

## Core implication

Durable meaning about a **UI definition** lives in **`UIDefinition`** (under `ir/`). External formats are adapters around it, not the source of truth.

`ir/` may later hold other IR kinds (for example layout IR). Each kind has its **own type name**. Do **not** name a type or file `IRDefinition` / `ir-definition`.

## Terminology in `.mdc` rules

When writing or editing project rules (`.mdc`), spell out project acronyms on use:

- Write **`SSOT (Single Source Of Truth)`** — do not use bare `SSOT` alone.
- Prefer the same pattern for other project acronyms when first introduced in a rule file.
